<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45321" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stellĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stēlĭo</span></b> ),
		ōnis, m.
		stella. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A newt</i>, <i>stellion</i> (having
			star-like spots on its back): Lacerto gecko, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 29, 4,
				28, § 90</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 26, 31, §
			91</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 4, 243</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 9, 7,
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a crafty</i>, <i>knavish person</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 30,
				10, 27, § 89</span></i>; <i><span class="en">App. M. 5,
				p. 172, 19</span></i>; cf. stellionatus.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
